{
  "_comment": [
    "Track props: everything beside and on a track that is not the track.",
    "",
    "A prop is data, so the same hay bale behaves identically on every stage and",
    "adding one means adding an entry here rather than writing a scene. Two",
    "kinds, and they are genuinely different things:",
    "",
    "  scenery  beyond the barrier. Drawn, never collided with, scattered",
    "           automatically by theme. Cheap enough to have thousands of.",
    "  hazard   on the racing surface. Collided with, and hitting one has a",
    "           consequence - that is why it is there. mass_kg decides whether",
    "           it is knocked aside or stops you, speed_penalty is how much",
    "           speed a hit scrubs, damage is what it does to the bodywork.",
    "",
    "'themes' restricts a prop to the stages it suits; empty means anywhere.",
    "Themes come from a track's own 'theme' field, defaulting to its surface."
  ],
